INT. BAGGAGE CLAIM - REGIONAL AIRPORT - NIGHT

A dead carousel. A single fluorescent tube flickers. The rubber flaps hang like black tongues.

CASSIAN MOORE (40s, rumpled suit, a battered suitcase at his feet) stands beside the carousel and does not look at it. MIRELLE DUPONT (30s, airport security, radio on her shoulder) enters from the staff door. OBADIAH FLYNN (60s, janitor, a mop and a yellow bucket) is already there, mopping where nothing has been spilled.

Mirelle drops her hand to her holster. Cassian lifts his palms. Obadiah keeps mopping, but slower.

MIRELLE
Sir, this area is closed.

CASSIAN
I was told to wait here.

MIRELLE
By whom?

CASSIAN
That's the problem. I don't know.

MIRELLE
Is that your bag?

CASSIAN
It came out of the last flight. The tag has my name. I don't remember packing it.

OBADIAH
(not looking up)
Nobody does.

MIRELLE
Sir, step away from the bag.

CASSIAN
I would love to, believe me. It keeps ticking.

Mirelle steps back. Obadiah lets go of the mop. It falls, and all three of them flinch at the clatter.

OBADIAH
Evening, Cassian.

CASSIAN
Do I know you?

OBADIAH
You will. Take your time. It's a long night.

MIRELLE
(into radio)
Control, I have a possible device in baggage claim, requesting a bomb squad.

Her radio answers with static, then a click, then silence.

MIRELLE (CONT'D)
Control? Control, do you copy?

OBADIAH
They can't hear you. The line's been cut since nine o'clock.

CASSIAN
Who are you?

OBADIAH
Just the janitor.

MIRELLE
Then why do you know the line is cut?

OBADIAH
Because I'm the one that cut it.

Mirelle draws. Cassian drops flat. Obadiah does not move, hands wide, smiling the way you smile at the end of a long shift.

OBADIAH (CONT'D)
Lower that, Miss Dupont. Nobody's getting hurt. We're going to have a conversation, the three of us, and when it's done, the bag will stop ticking.

MIRELLE
What conversation?

OBADIAH
About the flight you both worked on, eleven years ago.

CASSIAN
I never worked a flight.

OBADIAH
You didn't. You were a passenger. She was the gate agent who let you board.

Mirelle's gun hand wavers.

MIRELLE
That flight was...

OBADIAH
Go on.

MIRELLE
That flight was cancelled.

OBADIAH
Not for everyone.

The carousel lurches. It starts to turn. A single object rides out of the dark flap, a child's red shoe, and rotates slowly past the three of them before it vanishes again.
